course: dictionary
lesson: 4576
title: Using context: helmet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A helmet is a noun, a word for a thing. It is a hard hat that keeps your head safe. You can often work out a word's meaning from the words around it, which are its context.
explain: «A bike helmet sits snug and level, just above the eyebrows, with the strap buckled.» Snug, level and buckled tell you that a helmet is worn on the head and fastened under the chin, so it must be a kind of protective hat.
explain: The same word can mean something a little different in different lessons. In history, a helmet can be a metal hat worn by knights in battle. In sport and on bikes, it is a safety hat. The context tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Always wear a helmet when you cycle» still makes sense with "a hard hat that keeps your head safe", so your meaning is right.
fact: A helmet is a hard hat that keeps your head safe.
fact: Helmets are worn for bikes, scooters, horses, some sports, and jobs like building and firefighting.
fact: «Vikings did not wear horned helmets in battle; the horns come from costumes made for an opera in 1876.»
fact: «A helmet should sit level, about two fingers' width above the eyebrows.»
fact: Helmet is a noun. One helmet, two helmets.
exercise: What is a helmet? | A kind of bicycle bell | A soft hat for warm days | *A hard hat that keeps your head safe | A pair of gloves
exercise: «A bike helmet sits snug and level, just above the eyebrows.» Where should a bike helmet sit? | Pushed back to show the forehead | Down on the neck | *Level, just above the eyebrows | Over the ears only
exercise: Find and copy the word that names something you wear on your head. | safe | ride | eyebrow | *helmet
test: Why do firefighters and builders wear helmets? | To show they are on a team | To keep warm in the sun | To look taller | *To keep their heads safe
test: Which part of a helmet should be buckled? | The shell | *The chin strap | The stripe | The horns
exam: A helmet is a kind of hat, so what is the extra part of its meaning? | It has a brim to shade the sun | It is always blue | It is only worn by knights | *It is hard and keeps your head safe
